      "id": "lem-qc-random-measurement-stabilizer-update",
      "location": "Statement",
      "defect": "missing-hypothesis",
      "evidence": "The Statement allows any listed generators of S that stabilize a pure n-qubit state, but does not require them to be independent or S to have rank n. For n=2, take g1=g2=Z1, S=⟨Z1⟩, ψ=|00⟩, and M=X1. The hypotheses hold, but the update gives g′1=(-1)^bX1 and g′2=g2g1=I, which generate rank 1 rather than the claimed rank 2 subgroup. Proof [F5] asserts the old labels are independent, but the cited label-space lemma only says λ|S is injective and that dim L is independent of the generating list; it does not imply that this particular generating list is independent.",
